concern:
  heading: "Numbers, specs, and people who aren't at a computer"
  body: >
    <p>This industry runs on measurements, quantities, standards and prices, and a
    plausible-looking wrong number is worse than no number. We train the boundary hard:
    AI drafts the words around the numbers, a person owns the numbers themselves, and
    anything referencing a standard or a contract clause is checked against the source.
    It's a drafting assistant, and the discipline that keeps it one is part of the course.</p>
    <p>The second point shapes the whole program. Your people are on site, not at a desk,
    so every workflow we teach starts from a voice note or a photo on a phone. A process
    that requires sitting down at a laptop does not survive a real week, so we don't teach
    one.</p>
